---
import CapturePageLayout from "@layouts/CapturePageLayout.astro";
import CaptureHero from "@components/capture/CaptureHero.astro";
import CaptureSection from "@components/capture/CaptureSection.astro";
import CaptureTrialCta from "@components/capture/CaptureTrialCta.astro";
import CapturePricing from "@components/capture/CapturePricing.astro";
import PricingCalculator from "@components/capture/PricingCalculator.astro";
import Screenshot from "@components/Screenshot.astro";
import StepList from "@components/StepList.astro";
import Step from "@components/Step.astro";
import reviewBillImg from "@assets/capture/quickbooks/review-bill.png";
import { bulletList, inlineLink, subheading } from "@lib/capture-styles";

const description =
  "Otto reads your clients' receipts and bills, suggests categories from each client's own history, and publishes bills and supplier credits to QuickBooks Online.";

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: "With Otto", path: "/" },
  { name: "Otto Capture", path: "/capture/" },
  { name: "QuickBooks Online", path: "/capture/quickbooks/" },
];
---

<CapturePageLayout
  title="Receipt capture for QuickBooks Online"
  description={description}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  softwareApplication>
  <CaptureHero title="Receipt and bill capture for practices on QuickBooks Online">
    Otto reads every line of the receipts and bills your clients photograph,
    scan or forward, and suggests each category from how you've coded that
    client's suppliers before.
    <Fragment slot="after-cta">
      <p>
        You check each one, and Otto publishes it to the client's QuickBooks
        Online company as a bill or supplier credit, with the original attached.
        Capture publishes purchases to QuickBooks Online, not sales invoices.
        Nothing reaches QuickBooks until someone in your practice has reviewed
        it.
      </p>
    </Fragment>
  </CaptureHero>

  <CaptureSection
    title="Built by a practice, for practices"
    icon="hugeicons:building-03">
    <p>
      We run an accounting practice. We tried a lot of receipt capture tools,
      and none had the mix of features and pricing that worked for our clients.
      The small rough edges added up too, using them day in, day out.
    </p>
    <p>
      So we built Otto Capture around the jobs that took our time. Clients send
      documents without creating an account. And Otto reads every line and
      suggests a category from that client's own history.
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="What Otto does for your QuickBooks clients"
    tone="soft"
    icon="hugeicons:invoice-03">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Every line, not just the total</h3>
      <p>
        Otto reads the supplier, the dates, the totals and every line item on
        each document, as standard. A receipt with five different purchases on
        it reaches QuickBooks as a bill with five lines, each with its own
        category and VAT code, where some tools charge extra for line items.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Categories that learn each client's suppliers</h3>
      <p>
        Otto suggests a category for each line from how you've coded that
        client's bills from the same supplier. He learns one client at a time,
        from the bills you publish through Capture, including anything you
        changed in review, so his suggestions draw on more of that client's
        history as you go. For a supplier the client hasn't used before, he
        suggests a category from the document alone, and you decide.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4 pt-8">
      <h3 class={subheading}>Clients send documents without an account</h3>
      <p>
        Each client has their own email address, submission page and WhatsApp
        invite link, and you choose which to give them. Whoever holds the
        receipts just sends them. Nobody creates an account or installs
        anything, and you don't register anyone in advance.
      </p>
      <p class="text-base text-default-soft">
        Missing receipts isn't available for QuickBooks Online clients yet. If
        you'd like it for them, tell us, because it helps us decide what to
        build next.
      </p>
    </div>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection title="How it works" icon="hugeicons:route-01">
    <StepList>
      <Step>
        Your client sends a receipt or bill by email, through their submission
        page, or on WhatsApp.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        Otto reads it, matches the supplier to one of the client's QuickBooks
        suppliers, and suggests a category and VAT code for each line.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        Someone in your practice checks it and changes anything that needs it.
      </Step>
      <Step>
        You click <strong>Publish</strong>, and Otto creates the bill or
        supplier credit in the client's company, with the original document
        attached.
      </Step>
    </StepList>
    <Screenshot
      src={reviewBillImg}
      alt="A bill in review, each line with its own category and VAT code, ready to publish to QuickBooks Online"
    />
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="What lands in QuickBooks is what you checked"
    tone="soft"
    icon="hugeicons:document-validation">
    <p>A bill in the client's books should match the document it came from.</p>
    <ul class={bulletList}>
      <li>
        <strong>VAT read and checked line by line.</strong> Otto reads the VAT
        code and amount on each line, and checks the lines add up to the
        document's net, VAT and total. In review, a line whose VAT differs from
        its rate shows the rate's figure beside it, and a bill whose lines don't
        match its total is flagged before you publish. QuickBooks then records
        the VAT you approved.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Foreign currency at the client's own rates.</strong> With
        multi-currency on, a bill publishes in its own currency at the rate in
        the company's own exchange rate table, so it's valued the way the
        client's books value it. You can also convert a document to the amount
        that cleared the bank.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="Connecting a client's company"
    icon="hugeicons:plug-socket">
    <p>
      You connect each client's QuickBooks Online company to Capture on its own,
      so you can start with one client and add the rest when you're ready.
      Capture brings across that company's suppliers, chart of accounts, VAT
      codes and classes, so Otto's suggestions use that client's own lists from
      the first document.
    </p>
    <p>
      Capture uses the connection to create suppliers, bills and supplier
      credits, and to attach the original documents. It adds a currency to the
      company only when you choose to during review. The details are in{" "}
      <a
        href="https://support.withotto.app/capture/platforms/quickbooks/"
        class={inlineLink}>
        Otto Capture's QuickBooks Online guide
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureSection
    title="What it costs"
    tone="soft"
    width="default"
    icon="hugeicons:coins-01">
    <p class="max-w-3xl">
      Otto Capture is priced per client, per month, on three tiers. A client
      with no published documents in a month costs nothing. Each client sits on
      whichever tier is cheapest for what it published that month, and reaching
      a tier's allowance doesn't tip it into a bigger bill.
    </p>
    <CapturePricing variant="compact">
      <PricingCalculator />
    </CapturePricing>
    <p class="max-w-3xl pt-4">
      Full pricing is on{" "}
      <a href="/capture/#pricing" class={inlineLink}>
        the Otto Capture page
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </CaptureSection>

  <CaptureTrialCta title="Try it on as many QuickBooks Online clients as you like">
    <p>
      The free 30-day trial has no limit on clients or documents, so connect as
      many client companies as you like. We'd suggest putting Otto through his
      paces: include the clients whose paperwork takes longest each month, and
      send in a few weeks of their receipts and bills. Review them with every
      line already read and a category suggested, then publish them to
      QuickBooks.
    </p>
    <p>Otto Capture is available to UK accounting and bookkeeping practices.</p>
    <Fragment slot="note">
      Your clients can be on any mix of Xero, FreeAgent, and QuickBooks Online.
      On QuickBooks Online, Otto publishes purchases.
    </Fragment>
  </CaptureTrialCta>
</CapturePageLayout>
